      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq01_p01",
          "label": "a",
          "marks": 2,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq01_p01_c01",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "State P(X = 4.5) = 0."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq01_p01_c02",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "Explain that the probability at an exact single point is zero because an exact point has zero width, so P(X <= 4.5) = P(X < 4.5) + P(X = 4.5) = P(X < 4.5)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq02",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq02_p01",
          "label": "a",
          "marks": 2,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq02_p01_c01",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "State the mean mu = 80."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq02_p01_c02",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "Identify the variance sigma^2 = 25 and calculate the standard deviation sigma = sqrt(25) = 5."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_the_normal_distribution_m01_l01_drq03",
